---
import Downloads from "../components/Downloads.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { href, packs, ruleCount, source } from "../data/project";
const event = `{"schema_version":1,"agent":"claude","hook_event":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","phase":"pre","decision":"block","matched_rules":["protect-env-files"],"enforcement":"supported"}`;
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          <span class="signal-dot"></span> RUNTIME HOOKS. DEFENDER CONTEXT.
        </p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">
          Bring agent
          <br />
          actions <span>into focus.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-intro">
          AI agents use real tools. Give defenders a clearer view.
        </p>
        <p class="hero-description">
          Observe tool requests, apply readable YAML policies, and turn
          cooperative agent hooks into local evidence you can investigate.
          Also collect OTLP and provider audit observations.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="#downloads">
            Download now <Icon name="arrow" size={17} />
          </a>
          <a class="text-link" href={href("getting-started/#source")}>
            Build from source <Icon name="arrow" size={16} />
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-agents">
          <span>NATIVE HOOK ADAPTERS</span>
          <strong>Claude Code</strong>
          <i></i>
          <strong>Codex</strong>
          <i></i>
          <strong>Hermes</strong>
          <i></i>
          <strong>Gemini CLI</strong>
        </div>
        <p class="small-note">
          Plus Cursor, Copilot CLI and experimental Cowork. Seven native adapters,
          with <a href={href("telemetry/")}>eleven observation-only telemetry sources</a>.
          Coverage depends on the client and event; Cowork Desktop/VM execution remains unvalidated.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div
        class="event-console"
        aria-label="Illustrative synthetic hook events"
      >
        <div class="console-head">
          <span class="console-dots">
            <i></i>
            <i></i>
            <i></i>
          </span>
          <span>agent-lens / events.jsonl</span>
          <span class="mono-chip">DEMO</span>
        </div>
        <div class="console-status">
          <span>
            <span class="signal-dot"></span> TOOL ACTIVITY
          </span>
          <span>SYNTHETIC REPLAY</span>
        </div>
        <div class="event-row">
          <span class="event-time">12:04:21</span>
          <span class="event-icon allow">
            <Icon name="check" size={17} />
          </span>
          <div>
            <strong>
              Read <span>src/main.rs</span>
            </strong>
            <small>claude · PreToolUse</small>
          </div>
          <span class="decision allow">allow</span>
        </div>
        <div class="event-row selected">
          <span class="event-time">12:04:22</span>
          <span class="event-icon block">
            <Icon name="shield" size={17} />
          </span>
          <div>
            <strong>
              Write <span>.env.local</span>
            </strong>
            <small>claude · PreToolUse</small>
          </div>
          <span class="decision block">block</span>
        </div>
        <div class="console-detail">
          <span class="code-comment">
            // a rule match, with content omitted
          </span>
          <code>
            <span class="syntax-key">"matched_rules"</span>: [
            <span class="syntax-string">"protect-env-files"</span>],
            <br />
            <span class="syntax-key">"enforcement"</span>:{" "}
            <span class="syntax-string">"supported"</span>
          </code>
        </div>
        <div class="event-row">
          <span class="event-time">12:04:23</span>
          <span class="event-icon audit">
            <Icon name="lens" size={17} />
          </span>
          <div>
            <strong>
              Read <span>.env</span>
            </strong>
            <small>codex · PostToolUse</small>
          </div>
          <span class="decision audit">would_block</span>
        </div>
        <div class="console-foot">
          <span>
            <i></i> LOCAL JSONL
          </span>
          <span>METADATA FIRST. CONTENT OPT-IN.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="metrics" aria-label="Project at a glance">
      <div>
        <strong>
          {ruleCount}
          <span> / YAML rules</span>
        </strong>
        <p>5 defaults + 25 optional recipes</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>
          7<span> / native adapters</span>
        </strong>
        <p>Client and event coverage varies</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>
          3<span> / desktop platforms</span>
        </strong>
        <p>Windows · Linux · macOS</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <section class="section downloads-section" id="downloads" aria-labelledby="downloads-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">DOWNLOAD. EXTRACT. TRY IT.</p>
          <h2 id="downloads-title">Get AI Lens for your OS.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Grab a portable ZIP, then run the local demo. No Rust toolchain needed.</p>
      </div>
      <Downloads />
      <a class="text-link" href={href("getting-started/#downloads")}>Extraction and setup instructions <Icon name="arrow" size={16} /></a>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="flow-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">FOLLOW THE ACTION</p>
          <h2 id="flow-title">
            From tool request to
            <br />
            defender evidence.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Understand the decision at the hook boundary, then carry that context
          into your investigation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-grid">
        {[
          [
            "01",
            "terminal",
            "Observe the request",
            "An installed agent hook launches AI Lens with a native JSON callback.",
          ],
          [
            "02",
            "code",
            "Evaluate your policy",
            "Explicit tool, path, and content selectors match the original input.",
          ],
          [
            "03",
            "shield",
            "Return a decision",
            "Supported pre-tool hooks can request denial. Post-tool matches stay observational.",
          ],
          [
            "04",
            "layers",
            "Keep the evidence",
            "One event per JSONL line, ready for your existing log shipper and SIEM.",
          ],
        ].map(([number, icon, title, text]) => (
          <article class="flow-card">
            <div class="card-top">
              <Icon name={icon} size={24} />
              <span>{number}</span>
            </div>
            <h3>{title}</h3>
            <p>{text}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
    <section
      class="section catalog-section"
      id="catalog"
      aria-labelledby="catalog-title"
    >
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">READ IT. QUESTION IT. ADAPT IT.</p>
          <h2 id="catalog-title">
            A small policy catalog.
            <br />A practical starting point.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <a class="text-link" href={href("rules/#packs")}>
          Open rule reference <Icon name="arrow" size={16} />
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="catalog-grid">
        {packs.map((pack) => (
          <a class="catalog-card" href={href(`rules/#${pack.slug}`)}>
            <div class="card-top">
              <span class="pack-number">{pack.number}</span>
              <span class="rule-count">{pack.count} RULES</span>
            </div>
            <span class="card-category">{pack.category}</span>
            <h3>
              {pack.title}
              <Icon name="arrow" size={17} />
            </h3>
            <p>{pack.description}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="section-note">
        One policy file is loaded at a time. Optional packs are selected
        explicitly; combine chosen rule lists manually.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="section evidence-section" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">USE THE TOOLS YOU ALREADY HAVE</p>
        <h2 id="evidence-title">
          Readable events.
          <br />
          <span>Useful context.</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          Agent, tool, phase, matched rules, and enforcement support travel
          together. Raw prompts and tool content stay out of normal collection
          by default.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href={href("getting-started/#evidence")}>
          Take JSONL into your SIEM <Icon name="arrow" size={16} />
        </a>
      </div>
      <div>
        <CodeBlock
          code={event}
          lang="json"
          label="Illustrative event · content omitted"
        />
        <div class="evidence-tags">
          <span>allow</span>
          <span>block</span>
          <span>would_block</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <aside class="boundary-note">
      <Icon name="shield" size={26} />
      <div>
        <h3>A hook decision is one piece of the defense.</h3>
        <p>
          AI Lens is an educational project, not an OS sandbox. Prevention
          depends on a supported callback and a client that honors it. Keep
          agent approvals and OS controls in place; verify outcomes through your
          actual client.
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>
    <section class="closing-cta">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">BUILD YOUR UNDERSTANDING</p>
        <h2>
          Start with a demo.
          <br />
          Follow the evidence.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <a class="button primary" href={href("getting-started/#demo")}>
          Run the local demo <Icon name="arrow" size={17} />
        </a>
        <a class="text-link" href={source("CONTRIBUTING.md")}>
          Help improve the project <Icon name="external" size={15} />
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
